  "worked_solution": "We say that an implication has a *vacuous proof* if the antecedent is always false: \n\n$$\n\\overset{\\text{Always false}}{\\overset{\u23de}{P}}\u21d2\\,Q\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the consequent is true or false. \n\nWith that in mind, we proceed as follows:\n\nThe theorem can be written as the implication \n\n$$\n{m}^{2}-8m<-16\\,\u21d2\\,m\\le -4.\n$$\n\nNow, for each $m\\in Z,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-8m & =({m}^{2}-8m+16)-16 \\\\  & =(m-4)^{2}-16 \\\\  & \\ge -16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following fact:\n\nThe antecedent ${m}^{2}-8m<-16$ of our implication is always false.\n\nFinally, we can make the following conclusion:\n\nTherefore, the theorem is vacuously true.",
